{
  "id": "Compound::DB01045 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Rifampicin is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through a series of interconnected molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Rifampicin binds to Cyp3a43 and Cyp2b6, which in turn participate in metabolic pathways that are ultimately linked to Cyp2c8. Specifically, Cyp3a43 is involved in aromatase activity, which is a key step in the metabolic pathway leading to Cyp2c8. Similarly, Cyp2b6 is part of a metabolic pathway that is also linked to Cyp2c8. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Rifampicin influences Cyp2c8, likely through the modulation of enzyme activity or the induction of its expression. The integration of these pathways underscores a broader role for Rifampicin in modulating metabolic processes that ultimately affect Cyp2c8. The evidence supports a mechanism where Rifampicin exerts its effects through the activation or inhibition of metabolic pathways that are central to the function of Cyp2c8.",
